lane: like-for-like-lanes
why: the two rows where ZIO leads in the idiomatic table compare our
  ELEMENTWISE surface plus a MEMOIZING bridge against their
  chunk-native array walk -- mismatched on two axes at once.
    okayCollectionWhole: Source.of(list).toLazyList.foldLeft
    zioCollectionWhole:  ZStream.fromIterable(list).runSum
    okayChannelForeach:  Channel.buffer(1024)(list).drained.toLazyList.foreach
    zioChannelForeach:   ZStream.fromQueue(q).take(N).runForeach
  The tools for the honest pair already exist and were not used:
  Chunks.fromIterator is chunk-native, Source.runForeach consumes
  without memoizing. Until the fair lane is measured, any work on
  Drain aims at a gap of unknown size.
how: add the fair lanes, KEEP the old ones, and rename every lane in
  this benchmark so its granularity and whether it memoizes are in
  the name -- the third appearance of this same error (6b, the
  guarantee table, here) says the fix is a naming rule, not another
  one-off correction.
